-- The Ambassador program for everyone, the talent bench and the shop (LOCKED by Sean 2026-10-29: "lock it"). Concept session with V;
-- canon canon-ve-ambassadors-talent-shop, playbook ve-ambassadors-talent-shop. Updates canon-ve-pathways: Content Creators is a lead
-- source for Ambassadors, not its own program. Nothing is built yet: this records the decision.
insert into public.knowledge_records (slug, title, category, subcategory, status, owner, always_load, load_priority, tags, version, created_by, updated_by, change_summary, body)
select 'canon-ve-ambassadors-talent-shop',
  'Vegans Explore: one Ambassador program for everyone, a talent bench by results, and the LESARUSS.ai shop (LOCKED by Sean 2026-10-29)',
  'decisions', 'partners', 'active', 'sar', false, 50,
  array['vegans-explore','lesaruss-ai','ambassadors','creators','talent','services','pricing','bounties','campaigns'], 1, 'v', 'v',
  'Locked with V''s defaults (Sean: "lock it").',
  jsonb_build_object(
    'sean', 'Sean, 2026-10-29: "this shouldn''t become... the far end of the ambassador program... the ambassador program being for everyone and you fitting in based off of your results"; "these prices will be coming from LESARUSS.ai... any discount will come from them using points... points will come from them having provided services of their own to help promote what we''re doing"; "a shop... if they choose this, this is what happens... We can''t activate them... until they complete these steps"; "turn into a marketing agency for the 21st century"; "my role is to build the platform, put people into position, and make it run like a clean system."',
    'one_program', 'One Ambassador program for everyone. Never a separate Creators program. Each Ambassador carries a profile the team sets quietly (Balanced, Animals first, Community builder, Creator, Health and fitness) and can change in the background; the profile words their Guide and messages. In Pathways, Content Creators is a lead finder feeding the Ambassador pathway with the Creator profile set.',
    'results', 'They climb by results: the levels (1 to 4 on lifetime points), the jobs they take, the campaigns they finish. Doing little is fine; the far end of the ladder is paid work.',
    'jobs', 'One Opportunities board, three kinds of jobs: points jobs open to every Ambassador (post, share the link, show up); perk jobs (a dinner, a ticket, often for a cause, plus points); paid jobs by invitation only, for active Ambassadors with a rate card. From Level 2, bounties include professional work (managing a social account, editing, design, outreach), skill tagged, with a small paid trial job to vet.',
    'activation', 'Paid work needs activation, a self-updating checklist: 1. profile (photo, bio, what they do), 2. platforms (Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, podcast; numbers read where we can, else marked self-reported), 3. rates (post, reel, story, appearance, hosting, a day of social work; team only, updatable any time), 4. get paid (Stripe Connect hosted onboarding: bank and identity; the W-9 and 1099s through Stripe''s W-8/W-9 product, in preview, to be requested, else Stripe''s manual W-9 request). Not active yet until all four; reminders Day 2, Day 7, then weekly naming what is missing; a notification and Active when done.',
    'scouting', 'For active Ambassadors we scout like a talent roster (a Captiv8-style marketplace): our own campaigns, dinners, events and tours first; HARO (free daily reporter requests, relaunched by Featured.com in 2025) matched to people by topic; other marketplaces only as heads-ups from publicly posted opportunities, never scraping logged-in platforms.',
    'agency', 'We are the producer. A brand brings a goal and budget; we pick the talent from rate cards, reach and city (a brand may hand-pick for a fee), quote, collect at least the creator fees up front (held, not spent, until delivered: the locked LESARUSS.ai deposit rule), pay creators 50% on yes and 50% when their posts are live and checked, and produce the whole thing. A creator always gets their full rate. Sponsored posts carry the FTC disclosure. Rates and numbers stay with the team; a brand sees the package, names only after a creator says yes.',
    'shop', 'The shop is the LESARUSS.ai service list (one price list for every brand), open to members. Every item runs a workflow once picked: intake form, deposit (points up to half), job assigned, a Community Manager confirms dates, delivery, sign-off. Every service is offered two ways: AI-led (faster, cheaper) and people-led (vetted Vegan professionals from our community, about 1.5 times the AI-led price). Custom agency engagements stay quoted per project (brand-lesaruss-ai-positioning-model).',
    'rate_card', 'AI-led list prices, under market on purpose: press release written and pitched to a targeted media list $500 (market small-agency packages $1K to 5K); ongoing PR outreach $750 a month (small-business retainers $2K to 10K); social media management, one platform, $400 a month (basic $500 to 1,500); brand or product launch quoted per project from $1,500; campaign production 25% on top of creator fees, plus 10% when the brand hand-picks (agencies average about 30% of creator spend, ANA 2026). Members (Partners, Diplomats, Ambassadors Level 2 and up) save 20%. Points: 1 point = 1 cent, earned by promoting us, covering up to half of any service. Prices may be tuned to delivery cost before each service opens.',
    'partner_plan', 'The $111 quarterly Partner plan is on us for any Ambassador with the Creator profile at Level 2 and up while active (their link on their profile or bio and one share a quarter, checked quarterly).',
    'commission', 'Ambassadors with the Creator profile earn 20% from day one, then climb the member ladder to 30%.',
    'promise', 'We make it right: if a professional fails to deliver, we finish it ourselves and stop working with them. Refunds stay deposit only (the locked LESARUSS.ai delivery guarantee).',
    'people', 'The Community Manager is the client''s one contact and the face of the company. Professionals are independent contractors: our rules set standards and deadlines for what is delivered, never their hours or methods; a labor attorney reviews the contractor agreement once.',
    'reveal', 'Bit by bit. Now: the door (the Guide, the account, the profile, the checklist). Then one service at a time, each with its case study and a Daily Pulse announcement: books (Bob Leonard, then Brooke), courses (Dr. Klaper), event promotion (our events), then PR, then social, then brand launch.',
    'first', 'Torre Washington (his People page and channel are built). Gabriela Reyes: confirm her name and handle; the platform comes before the ask (feature her first, send the platform on her own tracked link, ask only on real interest). Then a city''s creators ahead of a dinner there, Philly first.',
    'build', 'The Creator Guide from Sean''s Canva Vegan Content Creator Survival Guide (design DAGx86FyHyw); profile claim and the activation checklist; the Opportunities board (points and perk jobs first, paid by hand); Stripe Connect payouts and campaign production; the shop on LESARUSS.ai, one service at a time; the lead finder by city.',
    'playbook', 've-ambassadors-talent-shop')
where not exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_records where slug = 'canon-ve-ambassadors-talent-shop');

update public.knowledge_records
set body = body || jsonb_build_object('creators', 'Content Creators is not its own program (Sean, 2026-10-29): it is a lead finder for the Ambassador pathway, the Creator profile set. See canon-ve-ambassadors-talent-shop.'),
  version = version + 1, updated_by = 'v', updated_at = now(),
  change_summary = 'Content Creators folds into Ambassadors as a lead source (Sean 2026-10-29).'
where slug = 'canon-ve-pathways' and not (body->>'creators' like 'Content Creators is not its own program%');

insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-ambassadors-talent-shop', 'vegans-explore', 'V',
  'Locked by Sean 2026-10-29 ("lock it"). One Ambassador program for everyone; Creator is a profile the team sets and can change; Content Creators in Pathways is a lead finder for it. People climb by results. One Opportunities board: points jobs (everyone), perk jobs (dinners, tickets, causes), paid jobs (invited, active Ambassadors with a rate card); from Level 2, professional bounties with a paid trial job. Paid work needs activation: profile, platforms, rates, get paid (Stripe Connect; W-9 and 1099s through Stripe), reminders Day 2, Day 7, weekly; Active when done. We scout for active people: our campaigns, HARO, public posts elsewhere (never scraping). We produce campaigns: we pick talent (brands may hand-pick for 10% more), creators get their full rate, 50% on yes and 50% on delivery, brand pays creator fees up front, our fee 25% on top. The shop is the LESARUSS.ai service list: every item a workflow (intake, deposit, assignment, Community Manager, delivery, sign-off), AI-led or people-led (about 1.5x). AI-led rate card: press release $500, PR outreach $750/mo, social one platform $400/mo, brand launch from $1,500 quoted; members save 20%; points (1 cent each) cover up to half. Partner plan on us for Creator-profile Ambassadors at Level 2 and up while active; 20% commission from day one. We make it right; refunds deposit only. Community Manager is the client''s face; contractors judged on deliverables, never hours. Reveal one service at a time with its case study and a Daily Pulse announcement: books, courses, event promotion, PR, social, brand launch. First: Torre Washington; Gabriela Reyes after the platform comes first; then Philly''s creators. Canon canon-ve-ambassadors-talent-shop.',
  'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-ambassadors-talent-shop' and kind = 'decision');
